p(30,8,"I well remember one spring evening I and Rory had been out",
 "Rory and Black Beauty meet a gig coming fast round a corner. The shaft of the gig runs into Rory's chest, and Rory is badly hurt.",
 "I remember well one spring evening when Rory and I had been out for the day. Rory was the horse that mostly went with me when a pair was asked for, and he was a good honest fellow. We had our own driver, and he was always kind and careful with us, so we had a very nice day. We were coming home at a good fast pace, about twilight. Our road turned sharp to the left. But we were close to the hedge on our own side and there was plenty of room to pass, so our driver did not pull us in. As we got near the corner, I heard a horse and two wheels coming quickly down the hill toward us. The hedge was high and I could see nothing, but the next moment we were upon each other. Luckily for me, I was on the side next to the hedge. Rory was on the left side of the pole, and he did not even have a shaft to protect him. The man driving was heading straight for the corner, and when he saw us he had no time to pull over to his own side. The whole shock came upon Rory. The shaft of the gig ran right into his chest and made him stagger back with a cry that I shall never forget. The other horse was thrown onto his back legs and one shaft was broken. It turned out that it was a horse from our own stables with the high-wheeled gig that the young men liked so much.",
 ["twilight","shaft","gig","haunches","stagger","stables"])
